# ONE settings file for the whole project.
#
#   1. Copy this file to `.env` (same folder, name exactly `.env`).
#   2. Change what you need. Lines starting with # are ignored.
#   3. Do not create other .env files (server/.env and app/.env.local are not used).
#
# `.env` is private and git-ignored. Never commit it or paste it in chat.

# ── Solana network ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Relay runs on devnet: Solana's free test network, tokens with no value.
# The server and the website both read this, so they always agree.
NETWORK=devnet

# ── Optional: the defaults work, change only if you need to ────────────
# A devnet RPC URL from a provider such as Helius (devnet plan). Empty uses the free public one,
# which is rate limited.
# SOLANA_RPC_URL=

# A hosted database (for example Neon). Empty uses the local Docker one:
#   docker compose -f compose.dev.yaml up -d
# DATABASE_URL=
# With a pooled URL above, put the direct (non-pooled) one here for migrations.
# DATABASE_DIRECT_URL=

# The address you open the website on. Only change it if you use another port.
# APP_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173

# Which creators the feed lists. Comma-separated wallet addresses. Anyone can publish a plan to a
# public network, so a deployment open to the internet should set this. Plans from other wallets
# stay reachable by direct link and are marked "Unlisted". Empty lists every plan.
# CREATOR_ALLOWLIST=

# A free key from Jupiter (portal.jup.ag) lifts the keyless rate limit on reference prices.
# JUPITER_API_KEY=

# Google sign-in, which following a plan needs (Discover and Watch need no account). Create an
# OAuth client of type "Web application" in Google Cloud Console. Its authorised redirect URI must
# equal GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI exactly. Empty turns sign-in off, and with it following.
#   local development:  http://localhost:5173/api/auth/google/callback
#   hosted:             https://<DOMAIN>/api/auth/google/callback
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=

# ── Only on the server that runs Docker Compose ────────────────────────
# Your domain, pointing at the server: a bare host name, no https:// and no slash.
# DOMAIN=relay.example.com
# Password for the Postgres container. Not needed if DATABASE_URL is set.
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
